:INFO
Art. 27 Return of forfeited cultural property
(Art. 28 CPTA)
1 Forfeited cultural property must be returned to its country of origin.
2 The FOC decides on the return. It may suspend the execution of the return until the return no longer poses a risk to the cultural property.
3 Forfeited cultural property shall be stored in a suitable facility designated by the FOC.
4 Forfeited assets shall be used by the FOC for:
a. granting financial assistance under Article 14, CPTA;
b. covering the costs of safeguarding and returning cultural property.
|

:NOTE
Art. 27 — Inserted by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).
Para. 3 — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).
|

:INFO
Art. 27a Exceptions to the return obligation
1 If return to the country of origin is not possible because the country does not wish the property to be returned or because the property cannot be assigned to a specific country, the cultural property may:
a. be given to suitable institutions for research or education purposes; or
b. be destroyed in a controlled manner if this is justified by the property’s negligible significance or its advanced state of decay.
2 The FOC shall draw up a related plan; this plan shall require the approval of the Federal Department of Home Affairs.
|

:NOTE
Art. 27a — Inserted by No I of the O of 15 Oct. 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 634).

